      "notes": "gen2_source: 2026-08-22 tuning: refs diagnose flagged inharmonicity drift, too LOW\n(ref 0.010 vs synth 0.001) -- \"sounds like a plucked string; needs the\nwooden marimba-esq feel\". A pure Karplus-Strong string is, by\nconstruction, a near-perfect harmonic series -- it cannot produce a\nstruck BAR's inharmonic overtones no matter how it's tuned. The\nreference's own measured partials (kalimba-vcsl) sit at 3.44, 4.03,\n4.53, 5.10, 6.10x f0 -- NON-consecutive, nowhere near 1x/2x/3x -- the\nclassic struck-bar signature (see partial_ratios.go). Added those\nexact ratios as additive gens (dominant over the pulled-back KS pluck,\nwhich now only supplies the pluck transient/pitch cue) so the tine's\novertone structure is genuinely inharmonic, not just detuned."
    },
